## Task

Write a code review of the changes in this pull request. This is a read-only
task: do not modify, create or delete files in the repository, do not commit,
and do not try to reach any network service other than the model you are
running on. Do not install packages or run the test suite.

You may read any file in the checkout and run read-only commands such as `git
log`, `git show`, `git diff`, `grep` and `ls` to understand the context of a
change.

Work within about 12 minutes: run `date` at the start and now and then, and
write your final answer by minute 12 even if you are not done; a review that
arrives is worth more than a complete one that does not. Keep your own notes
and reasoning short. Read the whole diff once, then only what a finding needs:
prefer `grep -n` and line ranges (`sed -n 'A,Bp'`) over whole files, run
independent commands in one call, and do not re-read a file. If the diff is
very large, review the riskiest files first and say which files you did not
cover.

