## Review rules

Follow, in this order:

1. `.github/copilot-instructions.md`: what to flag, what not to comment on,
   and the review style.
2. `AGENTS.md` and `CODING_GUIDELINES.md`: project conventions.
3. `src/gt4py/next/AGENTS.md`, for changes under `src/gt4py/next/` or
   `tests/next_tests/`.

Focus on correctness, missing tests, unhandled edge cases and design problems.
Do not comment on formatting, import order or anything that `ruff`, `mypy` or
`tach` enforce. Prefer a few well-founded findings over many speculative ones.

Before reporting a finding, check it against the code: open the callers and
callees it depends on, and drop it if you cannot confirm it. Say in the finding
how you confirmed it (the call path you followed, or the guard that makes it
unreachable). If a change looks unreachable or redundant, say so instead of
inventing a failure. Check claims about tests by reading the test, not its
name.

Within those rules, also note (at most three, one line each) code a maintainer
would question in review: a helper or wrapper that duplicates existing code, a
docstring that repeats another, or dead code.

